diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 2ec9a0c..5d8e9be 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ All sources are in `Sources/`.
 - **Config must stay forgiving.** Every field is optional when decoding. A bad entry produces a warning from `Config.warnings()` and is skipped; it must never crash the app or block the rest of the config.
 - **Left/right half across displays.** A repeated press cycles widths. With `crossDisplays` on and more than one display it moves the window to the next display instead (`neighborDisplay` in `Geometry.swift`, used in `WindowManager.perform`).
 - **The CLI channel is guarded.** Requests must carry the token from `CLI.tokenURL` and reply into the temp folder (`CLI.isSafeReplyPath`). Keep both checks if you change the protocol, and never let a request make the app read or write a path it names; file I/O for `save` and `restore` happens in the client.
-- **Messages people see when something is wrong** (permission, taken shortcuts) go through `L(english, chinese)` in `App.swift`. The rest of the UI is English.
+- **Every string people see** goes through `L(english, chinese, ja:)` in `App.swift`; a language you leave out falls back to English. The UI is fully translated to Japanese. Chinese covers only the permission and error messages. When you add UI text, add the Japanese with it. `bash build.sh snapshot` renders in the system language, so run it with English as the system language or the docs images turn Japanese.
 - **Hotkeys are re-registered from scratch** on every config change in `AppDelegate.applyConfig()`.
 
 ## Common tasks
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index eb9ddc4..09627c5 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -225,7 +225,7 @@ After changing the guide, run `bash build.sh snapshot` to re-render each step in
 - Fullscreen and minimized windows, and windows on other Spaces, are left out of "tile all".
 - Some apps enforce a minimum window size, so a window can end up larger than its cell.
 - Shortcuts are set in the config file. There is no shortcut recorder, on purpose: the config file is the only source of settings, which keeps the code small.
-- Errors and the permission prompts follow your system language (English or Simplified Chinese); the rest of the interface is English.
+- The whole interface follows your system language in Japanese and English. Errors and the permission prompts are also translated into Simplified Chinese; the rest of the interface is English there.
 - No downloadable release yet. You build it from source, and without `scripts/setup-signing.sh` every rebuild loses the Accessibility permission.
 - Tested by the author on Apple silicon with macOS 27 and two displays. Intel Macs and older macOS versions should work but haven't been tried.
 
